# Use mq-deadline with a deep 4MB read-ahead on the SD/eMMC boot device. A
# handheld runs one game and the Steam UI, so BFQ's fairness between many
# processes buys little, while under it a small journal commit can take over a
# second on an SD card. Steam writes game recordings from its capture threads,
# so a commit that slow stalls the recording and leaves a clip Steam can't play.
# NOTE: scoped to mmcblk (the SD card novadeck boots from today). A future
# install-to-UFS target enumerates as scsi/sd*, not mmcblk, so it won't match
# this rule — revisit when the UFS install path lands.
ACTION=="add|change", KERNEL=="mmcblk[0-9]", ATTR{queue/scheduler}="mq-deadline", ATTR{queue/read_ahead_kb}="4096"
